@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# v0.3 response to the Gemini review
+
+This review was checked against the hash-verified delivered v0.2 ZIP, not an unidentified older checkout. Its source SHA-256 was `41cb8bf3592b0a2d500121e6bbaf732f0340c9f2a3e001affe05b29385b73049`; selected asset release was `160d0b52e9e00593fce83ab872967da45893a681af59455989bccc95dfad2575`, with conservative deployment mode. Existing v0.2 results are preserved under `evidence/v0_2`.
+
+## Claim-by-claim audit
+
+| Gemini concern | Verified evidence | Resolution in v0.3 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Learned policy is unpromoted because of illegal questions/budget overruns | All 120 v0.2 validation episodes were valid. Learned scored 21 versus conservative 15 MSMI pairs over the same 24 worlds. Four-block interval for gain included zero. No frozen final test or Docker pass existed. Illegal asks were not an observed cause. | Keep promotion blocked until evidence supports it. Fit a fixed regularization grid using training seeds only; report a fixed unseen-seed evaluation without test-driven tuning. |
+| One BLAS thread causes the 2-CPU container bottleneck | Official containers permit at most 2 CPUs; pure Python greedy inference does not use BLAS. One BLAS thread limits oversubscription in fitting/solver subprocesses. No Windows CPU profile established a bottleneck. | Keep legal resource limits. Record actual stage, call and Docker-family times. Protect downstream stages instead of assuming unsafe extra compute will solve it. |
+| Docker starts too late and cold pulls consume the budget | Confirmed scheduling weakness: validation preceded Docker, with only a cleanup reserve. | Check the Linux engine and prepare the base image before training. Assess conservative and learned containers before the long pilot. Reserve 20 minutes for the combined Docker stage and 5 minutes for pilot validation upstream; cap the full workflow at the requested wall budget. |
+| Container evidence needs real cryptographic signatures | The existing mechanism hashes content and records immutable image IDs. No signing key, trusted signer or signature requirement was configured by the public protocol. Host success does not prove sandbox compliance. | Label proof type explicitly. Never invent a signature. Preserve unverified status without actual Docker. A separate learned-container record is now mandatory for candidate promotion. |
+| NTFS bind mounts slow assessed inference | The pinned official `docker_command` mounts no source/data host volumes. NTFS overhead can affect host collection, cache and build context; that is separate from assessed container inference. | Provide native WSL Linux filesystem instructions and reduce Docker build context. No measured cross-platform speedup is asserted. |
+| Replace cache leases with PID locks | The lease is in `blackbox/storage.py`, not rollout `cache.py`. The workflow already had an OS-held lock. New episode owners could still wait 120 seconds after a hard kill. PID checks alone risk reuse and namespace ambiguity. | Add per-owner OS locks; process death releases the lock immediately. Preserve token ownership, heartbeats and stale-commit rejection. Transactionally migrate version-2 ledgers, retaining lease fallback for legacy owners and all attempt history. Real hard-kill tests exercise recovery. |
+
+## Architecture and scope
+
+The hackathon implementation remains an offline modular monolith with a trusted control plane for collection, fitting, verification and release selection. Inference receives only observations; immutable model/sampler bundles and exact source identities bind evidence. SQLite is a local experiment ledger, not a distributed queue. Keep its owner-lock directory on the same local filesystem. No Kubernetes, remote feature store, Redis or online model service is necessary for this offline CPU submission.
+
+Deployment selection is independent of fitting. Candidate quality gates remain a positive paired lower interval, at least ten independent seed blocks, no family mean MSMI regression and no more than five percentage points of information-group coverage decline. v0.3 additionally closes the gap that let a conservative Docker pass stand in for learned-policy sandbox validation. Nothing automatically promotes the model.
+
+The feature transform stays at the previously audited point-in-time schema. With only 53 positive training events, expanding feature dimensions or tuning an action threshold merely to clear a small pilot would need additional evidence. The implemented change selects joint/directional L2 penalties by leave-one-training-seed-out log loss, compares constant prevalence inside each fold, and records mature feature missingness, score quantiles and calibration. Predictive metrics do not substitute for MSMI policy outcomes.
+
+## Verification boundaries
+
+The authoring host provides Python 3.12 CPU execution but no Docker CLI/daemon or native Windows PowerShell. Real Docker Desktop/WSL2 execution remains necessary on the laptop. Hashes prove local content correspondence, not a trusted external certification. `results/REPORT.md` is generated from current evidence; current results are never inferred from older archived runs.
+
+`plans/REVIEW_PROTOCOL.md` declares a fixed ten-block final evaluation before this iteration's outcomes. Its plan is bound to final fitted assets before execution. Ten blocks satisfy the existing minimum count but are not claimed to be a powered sample. Seeds 3101-3110 become consumed test data after this review and must not be called unseen in later tuning.
+
+## Sources
+
+- Pinned starter source and protocol: `starter/SOURCE.json`, `starter/docs/POLICY_INTERFACE.md`, `starter/evaluate.py`, `starter/test_runner.py`.
+- Delivered evidence: `evidence/v0_2/REPORT.md`, `validation.json`, `release_readiness.json`.
+- [Docker WSL filesystem guidance](https://docs.docker.com/desktop/features/wsl/best-practices/).
+- [Docker CPU/memory limits](https://docs.docker.com/engine/containers/resource_constraints/).
+
+## Measured model diagnosis after fitting
+
+Fresh collection produced 3,385 mature joint labels with 53 positives (about 1.57%). Training took 244.2 seconds on the authoring host, including collection and grouped regularization selection. This is a host observation, not a Docker Desktop timing promise.
+
+Both heads selected L2=100 from the fixed grid. Equal-training-seed mean held-out joint log loss was 0.0814420 versus 0.0814568 for fold-fitted constant prevalence: only about 0.018% relative reduction. Directional log loss was 0.6597599 versus constant 0.6593687, about 0.059% worse. These comparisons are conditional on selected mature introductions; they do not establish population-level probability quality.
+
+For every soft field, approximately 68.4%-70.7% of training pair comparisons have at least one missing observation. Rare labels plus weak observed feature signal are a more concrete ML limitation than an unobserved illegal-question claim. Changing a threshold to force promotion would not resolve it. The directional head remains experimental and is not used by learned-greedy's pair score.
+
+The next research changes would require fresh evaluation: collect additional training-only seed blocks, compare point-in-time information-acquisition policies under equal compute/budget, and test whether better disclosed soft features improve mature ranking. Final seeds consumed in this iteration cannot be recycled as unseen data for those changes.
+
+## Completed pilot result
+
+The complete v0.3 pilot has 120/120 valid episodes and no failed attempts. Conservative scored 15 MSMI pairs, learned 18, on the same 24 worlds (0.3125 versus 0.3750 per 100 arrivals). The four-block descriptive gain interval is [-0.25, 0.25] per 100; it includes zero. Shift-family means are 0.5000 conservative versus 0.3750 learned. The prior v0.2 learned pilot scored 21; v0.3's improved regularization-selection procedure does not imply improved policy outcomes. No refit or threshold change follows this pilot in the frozen review protocol.
+
+## Final result and promotion decision
+
+All 120 frozen final episodes completed, with no failed attempts. Across ten seed blocks/six families, learned recorded **59 MSMI pairs** versus conservative **46** (0.4917 versus 0.3833 per 100 arrivals). The seed-block bootstrap gain interval is **[0.0000, 0.2333]** per 100; its lower bound is zero, so it does not clear the strict-positive gate.
+
+| Family | Conservative MSMI per 100 | Learned MSMI per 100 |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| development | 0.45 | 0.80 |
+| sparse | 0.05 | 0.05 |
+| cold_start | 0.30 | 0.15 |
+| delayed | 0.45 | 0.40 |
+| shift | 0.60 | 0.70 |
+| drift | 0.45 | 0.85 |
+
+Cold-start and delayed family regressions also fail the predeclared guardrail. Information-group coverage passed. Both Docker policies remain unverified because no Docker CLI or daemon socket exists on this host. Conservative remains the deployment default.
+
+The final run exposed a numerical bug in interval averaging: floating-point cancellation produced +2.8e-18 instead of zero. Exact rational arithmetic now prevents a false strict-positive flag. The original raw runs, pre-outcome plan and full execution source preimage are retained. An explicit analysis-only verifier proves that policy/model/simulator/feature/episode-execution code did not change; current-source analysis and original-source execution are labelled separately. No raw outcome or identity was rewritten, and the gate thresholds remain unchanged.
+
+Twelve additional host subprocess episodes (two policies x six families on exploratory seed 101) completed successfully: 1,440 fresh policy invocations. These verify restart-per-call host transport, not Docker resource compliance. The supervised host workflow took 1,002.0 seconds, the frozen final run 991.0 seconds and the subprocess checks 279.9 seconds. They partly overlapped and must not be added as elapsed wall time. Their combined phase allowances were 70 minutes, below the user's two-hour allocation; Windows/Docker timings remain unmeasured.
+
+## Current assessment
+
+**7/10 as an ML hackathon engineering prototype**, a qualitative judgment rather than a certification. The source/evidence controls, recovery, bounded execution and reproducible verification are considerably stronger. Readiness remains blocked by missing real Docker evidence and model quality gates. It is not honest to call all empirical issues solved: the weak observed feature signal, rare positive labels and two family regressions remain the ML research work. The unchanged conservative default is the appropriate result of the current gates.
